WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.602
 Dwight, Billy Bob,
congratulations.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.370
You made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.840
Now we're sending you back to
your home forges for five days

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.676
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history,

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:16.382
and that weapon
is the rhomphaia.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.285
Originating as early as
400 BC, the rhomphaia

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:21.154
was a fearsome weapon
prominently used

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.356
by Thracian tribes
of eastern Europe.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.326
It featured a long single-edged
blade that had great

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.594
cutting and slashing
strength due to the blade's

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.229
slightly forward curve.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.264
Usually forged
with iron, warriors

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:34.934
had to use two hands to
wield this heavy weapon using

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.036
an overhead sweeping
or hacking motion

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.971
to attack from close distances.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.540
First mentioned
in historical text

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.242
by the ancient Roman
historian Titus Livius.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.077
It was recorded as
one of the key weapons

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.012
in violent Thracian warfare.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.213
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.582
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:56.288 line:8%
 My name is Dwight Phillips,
and I was the first person

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.057 line:8%
from Tennessee
that I know of that

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.126 line:14%
passed the master-smith test.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.996
What I love about bladesmithing,
200 years from now,

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.498
somebody else is
going to be picking

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.933
it up and looking at it.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.868
That really satisfies me.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.003
It looks pretty good.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.306
The thing I'm worried
about is the handle.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.375
I went with a full tang, which
makes it a little bit heavier.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.244
I may have to drill
some holes in there

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.346
and take away some weight.

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:26.185
That made me a little nervous.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:29.923
Next, we will clay it and
get ready for heat treat.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.857
This will help keep
part of the metal soft,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.561
and the other part
will get hard.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:38.465
I feel really nervous about
quenching something this long,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.265
but what the heck?

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.601
Let's go see what happens.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:45.138
If this heat treat goes wrong,
I could be in serious trouble.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.641
The time it takes to work
out another sword this long,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.176
I'll be down and out.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.311
I'm more nervous
than a mouse that's

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.214
running from a cat on this.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.621
With no cracks in the
edge, and it wouldn't warp.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:02.755
It looks perfect.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:09.028
Let's check it out here.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.163
It's dragging right there.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.866
Kind of running out of time.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.600
If I don't get this
blade razor sharp,

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.236
Billy Bob could
take home the money.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.738
I have got to fix it.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.209
That's better.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.212
If I had a lot more time, I
could really stone this edge

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.014
and get it even
sharper than that.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.949
But I think it's going
to go through everything

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.217
they put up against it.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.519
We just had to see.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.757
 My name is Bill Saule.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.560 line:8%
Everybody in the knife
world calls me Billy Bob.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.562
I've been a master-smith
for eight years.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.064
When I decided to make a
knife, I'm just going to do it,

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.966
and there's not a
lot of planing to it.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.869
You just keep doing
it until it's a knife.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.805
The sword isn't fitting all
the way through the forge,

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:55.308
so I just made one renovation.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.143
I just knocked a
hole in the firewall.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.344
So I think I'm going to
make a simple pattern

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.214
of twisted Damascus, and
I can put it on the handle

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.317
and give it a little detail.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.451
Oh.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.853
Never pick a snowball
up in a blacksmith shop

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:11.457
because it could be hot.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.891
I'm way behind.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.293
This is no bull [bleep].

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.598
The handle is harder
than I expected.

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:22.268
Today, I'm going to try to
fit and shape the handle.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.736
Oh, yes, baby.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.103
I'm doing it in two pieces.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:28.607
It just adds to
the craftsmanship.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.409
Son of a bitch.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.745
The handle is looking a lot
better than I thought it would,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:36.615
but we're never out of the woods
until we send this bad boy off.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.918
[bleep] damn it.

00:03:38.984 --> 00:03:40.819
The [bleep] treads are crooked.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.923
Being a perfectionist, I'm
going to keep messing with it

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.191
till I get it right.

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:48.361
That may be the downfall
of this whole thing.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.296
 Master bladesmiths, to see
what kind of lethal damage

00:03:51.396 --> 00:03:53.499
your rhomphaias, we'll
take your rhomphaias

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.102
and deliver lethal
slashes and thrusts

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.070
on this wild boar carcass.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.171
Dwight, you're up first.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:03:59.905
Are you ready?

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.374
 I'm ready.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.076
 As you can see, I'm still
recovering from an injury,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.911
so to be my arm today,
I'd like to welcome

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:08.914
my brother, RJ Marcaida.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:12.919
[music playing]

00:04:27.766 --> 00:04:28.534
 Wow.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.711
 Well, Dwight, on
the initial draw cut,

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.914
it is sharp to where
it lacerated deep

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.482
into this wild boar carcass.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:47.719
On the thrust, it penetrated
easily into the carcass,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.923
and on the final cut right
here, your blade cut all

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:52.391
the way through the carcass.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.561
Overall, your
rhomphaia will kill.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.828
 Thank you.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:57.996
DOUG: Good job.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:04:59.298
All right, Billy Bob.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.968
 That's a hard act to
follow, but let's do it.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:05.972
[music playing]

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:18.784
 All right, Billy Bob.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.187
It's so light you can almost
wield it with one hand.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:24.223
The edge over here is
so sharp it lacerates

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.425
easily without much force.

00:05:26.491 --> 00:05:28.994
The profile you have
over here for thrusting

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:33.432
allowed it for a very deep,
quick in-out penetration.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.867
Overall, your
rhomphaia will kill.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.436
 Thank you.

00:05:37.502 --> 00:05:39.439
 Next up is the strength test.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.841
Tim.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.709
 Gentlemen, to test the
strength and durability

00:05:43.775 --> 00:05:46.312
of your blades, I'm going to
clamp them into this machine,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.647
and it will deliver a
strike on the sugar cane

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.716
of about 500 pounds of force.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.818
Remember, this test is all
about what the sugar cane

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.453
does to your blade and
not what your blade

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.888
does to the sugar cane.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.790
Dwight, I've already
clamped yours in.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:58.624
Are you ready to go?

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.258
 I'm ready.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.027
 3, 2, 1.

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:12.071
Well, Dwight, your
blade held up perfectly.

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.873
It's like it didn't
hit anything.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.774
It's still dead straight.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:16.308
Very well done.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.543
 Thank you.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.911
 Billy Bob, you're up next.
You ready?

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:19.612
 I can't wait.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.312
 All right.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:21.180
Let's do this.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.849
3, 2, 1.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:31.357
 Ah, you killed me.

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:33.893
 Well, Billy Bob, I
love the overall weight.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:37.797
It feels like it's a really good
chopper, and, most importantly,

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.966
the edge is still
as razor sharp as it

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.068
was when you brought it here.

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:42.801
Very well done.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:43.969
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:46.071
 Next up is the sharpness
test, and for that,

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.807
I give you to Dave.

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:49.642
 All right, gentlemen,
I'll be working

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.477
my way through this
rope maze by cutting.

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:53.779
We've seen your blades kill.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.481
Let's see if they've
held their edge.

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:56.815
Dwight, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:57.449
 I'm ready.

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:58.217
 All right.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.251
Let's do this.

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:02.922
[music playing]

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.072
All right, so, Dwight, your
blade is just pristine.

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:23.542
I mean, there's not a mark or a
hair hanging on it or anything.

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.911
Feel-wise, it's got a
lot of forward weight.

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:29.181
Makes for a very strong chop,
but I do have to stop it,

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.582
slow it down, and back it up.

00:07:30.682 --> 00:07:32.084
I think it's a beautiful weapon.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:32.818
 Thank you.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:33.986
Thank you.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:34.986
 All right, Billy Bob.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:35.855
You ready to go?

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:36.722
 Let's do it.

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:37.989
DAVE: OK.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.694
[music playing]

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:59.145
Billy Bob, this is sharp.

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:01.280
It blew through
rope like nothing.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.782
I felt I could really
control this weapon

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:06.885
just because it's so much
lighter up through here.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:07.753
Fabulous weapon.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.286
 Thank you.

00:08:08.353 --> 00:08:10.589
 Well done.

00:08:10.655 --> 00:08:14.060
 Dwight, Billy Bob,
both done masterful work

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.827
as expected from master-smiths.

00:08:15.927 --> 00:08:17.529
However, in this
arena of competition,

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.798
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:27.305
and that champion is Billy Bob.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.641
Congratulations.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.543
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.878
 Thank you.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:36.916
 Dwight, your blade was
bad-ass, but this time,

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.050
it didn't make the cut.

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:39.952
Doug Marcaida will explain.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:43.155
 Dwight, first of
all, this is exactly

00:08:43.256 --> 00:08:45.690
what we expect
for a final round,

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.194
two beautifully-matched blades.

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:50.229
But your blade is
slightly heavy.

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:51.730
That offsets its
balance compared

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:55.601
to Billy Bob's, and for that
reason we're sending you home.

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:59.704
Dwight, I need to ask you to
please surrender your blade.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.708
 Billy Bob winning
is no disgrace.

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:05.444
I believe both blades
are pretty equal.

00:09:05.544 --> 00:09:06.745
I'd hate to have been a judge.

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:09.314
Being on "Forged in
Fire" is one of the best

00:09:09.381 --> 00:09:10.783
experiences I've ever had.

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:13.118
If it's something that
you're passionate about,

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:16.221
you need to go for it.

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:17.756
 Billy Bob, congratulations.

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:19.624
You are the new "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:19.724 --> 00:09:22.060
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:23.195
Good job.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.463
 Thank you.

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.931
I'm honored to have
been here to do it.

00:09:25.997 --> 00:09:29.501
 Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:30.936
 The old man won
"Forged in Fire."

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:34.373
The old man come here and
kicked ass and took names.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.640
It feels good, man.

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:37.042
I'm proud of both of us.

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.344
Dwight and I forged
not only blades,

00:09:39.444 --> 00:09:40.713
but we forged a friendship.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.381
I'm going to go home
and take a break.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.783
I'm going to get
me a damn pedicure.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.588
You don't know what you're
missing if you ain't had one.

